{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/570983-advise-on-gifts","id":570983,"title":"Advise on gifts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-27T22:20:15-07:00","id":570983,"title":"Advise on gifts","content":"Would like some advice on good gifts to give in various situations<br /> <br /> am STing my first Salon, what would a good gift to a Promising Invictus fledgling be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T22:25:26-07:00","id":571013,"title":"","content":"Who is the gift giver, and what is known of the fledgling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T23:15:52-07:00","id":571032,"title":"","content":"Well Thinking on several potential gift givers,<br /> <br /> Thinking on a Daeva Primogen currently<br /> <br /> Whats known about the fledgling<br /> <br /> She was a bit young for the embrace, but not quite farcically so. at 15<br /> <br /> She has a very sharp native intelligence, and was actualy taking college classes at her age prior to the embrace. a few months ago.<br /> <br /> Her Sire ranking Ventrue invictus (now theres a rare combination Lol!) Is relatively fond of her.<br /> <br /> Shes minding her manners since her initial presentation, but this is the first chance to really interact with her..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T00:38:37-07:00","id":571071,"title":"","content":"If you want to be practical more than anything else, a fake ID would probably be very useful, helping her get into clubs to feed without having to rely on dominate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-28-2015, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T11:10:54-07:00","id":571698,"title":"","content":"ideas on symbolism in what a gift can mean?<br /> <br /> one idea I have is that a chess set can mean that a contest of wits is about to begin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T17:22:49-07:00","id":572020,"title":"","content":"Non-material things can make good gifts too. Inviting the fledgeling to hunt at a club or other location that's otherwise considered part of the Elder's territory could be a powerful show of favor, while also giving the Elder an opportunity to meet the fledgeling again, privately, in an environment the Elder controls. An influential vampire with a particular interest in the fledgeling might even cede her a modest feeding ground, though the player should probably buy it with experience if they're interested in the character keeping it for the long term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T17:48:57-07:00","id":572040,"title":"","content":"Something that once belonged to a promising member of the Invictus' past in that area might be a nice sort of back-handed compliment and warning. A nice pair of glasses that may help to ostensibly make her look older but belonged to a young firebrand who had to be put out to the sun. A journal from a wisened and educated vampire who went mad at his inability to stay in touch with the academic life as much as he wanted. Things like that are more about the story, but can also have plot hooks attached.<br /> <br /> Yeah a chessboard could mean entering a competition, or a need to sharpen mental skills and think ahead, or an unspoken way to say they can invite the gift giver over, providing they're a chess player, or just to talk, maybe as a mentor. There's a lot of ways to handle symbolic gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-28-2015, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T09:06:56-07:00","id":628712,"title":"","content":"Hmmmn<br /> <br /> On the finer points of a gift?<br /> <br /> On a revolver, Thinking, what kind of handle, trigger, etc it should have... Thinking about a Fancy gold or silver plated revolver, but not sure what that could signify.<br /> <br /> or a jeweled dagger.<br /> <br /> or different symbolism to a ruby ring, from an emeral tiara.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 08-16-2015, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T11:52:32-07:00","id":891289,"title":"","content":"thought id go ahead and necro this thread, as the question on gifts as a form of subtle communication is important, and difficult.<br /> <br /> oh was just thinking<br /> <br /> Hmmmn you think 23 pieces of Silver a good snub, at someone who you see as perfidious, or think it will just be &quot;Money, gee thanks&quot; <br /> <br /> noticed a lot of things available on Amazon...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T05:27:23-07:00","id":891677,"title":"","content":"Really depends on the person. A devout and educated Christian, yeah. 99% of the world, no. Unless they're really rich and are only seeing the value and going &quot;but this is like nothing?&quot; unless the silver is in and of itself remarkable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T09:52:48-07:00","id":891818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/570983-advise-on-gifts?p=891289#post891289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thought id go ahead and necro this thread, as the question on gifts as a form of subtle communication is important, and difficult.<br /> <br /> oh was just thinking<br /> <br /> Hmmmn you think 23 pieces of Silver a good snub, at someone who you see as perfidious, or think it will just be &quot;Money, gee thanks&quot; <br /> <br /> noticed a lot of things available on Amazon...</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a lot of inferences that could be made depending on the context of the gift.<br /> As an educated Christian, I can say that if the giver is inferring that the recipient is an embezzling thief who will betray his friends is symbolized by twenty three pieces of silver, the gift giver (or if the recipient gets offended) is displaying their ignorance because it was the Pharisees who took 30 silver from the church treasury to pay Judas Iscariot (already known for embezzling). Thirty silver is also the price one paid if someone accidentally killed a slave according to Mosaic law.<br /> It may be seen as a warning (or threat) to the recipient not to betray the trust placed in them or they could end up in an anonymous grave.<br /> If the gift giver is a high up official or law enforcement type, it could be construed as a statement that he expects the recipient to inform on his associates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 05-16-2016, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T11:16:55-07:00","id":891874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/570983-advise-on-gifts?p=891818#post891818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thirty silver is also the price one paid if someone accidentally killed a slave according to Mosaic law.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oof. If they get the reference, that would make a hell of a &quot;polite&quot; rimshot after making official restitution for killing another's <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">intimate </span></span></span>ghoul or mortal.<br /> <br /> &quot;Fine, here's your damn property deed. Since we're already here, I got you a little something extra-&quot; <br /> <br /> *clattering*<br /> <br /> *frenzy*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T11:10:12-07:00","id":893457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/570983-advise-on-gifts?p=891818#post891818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are a lot of inferences that could be made depending on the context of the gift.<br /> As an educated Christian, I can say that if the giver is inferring that the recipient is an embezzling thief who will betray his friends is symbolized by twenty three pieces of silver, the gift giver (or if the recipient gets offended) is displaying their ignorance because it was the Pharisees who took 30 silver from the church treasury to pay Judas Iscariot (already known for embezzling). Thirty silver is also the price one paid if someone accidentally killed a slave according to Mosaic law.<br /> It may be seen as a warning (or threat) to the recipient not to betray the trust placed in them or they could end up in an anonymous grave.<br /> If the gift giver is a high up official or law enforcement type, it could be construed as a statement that he expects the recipient to inform on his associates.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Any verses you can cite on Judas embezzling, so I know it's not a thing like Noah being laughed at by neighbour's, for building a ship on dry land, something that everyone has heard of, but with NOTHING in the bible to back it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T13:12:25-07:00","id":893541,"title":"","content":"Gospel of John chapter 12 verse 6 outright calls him a thief who took money from the moneybag for his own personal use.<br /> The assertion that Noah was mocked because it had never before rained is an apocryphal claim. It's partially derived because Jesus himself said that the people of Noah's era went about their business heedless of his warning and the gradual completion of the ark right until the day the deluge started.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T06:21:44-07:00","id":896047,"title":"","content":"Wow...Rare I run into someone this educated, any thoughts on using the story of king Mannaseh as inspiration for a game?<br /> <br /> He lived a life. Of decadence and sin, was conquered and carried away in chains.. <br /> <br /> Then humbled himself before the God of his father's and saw his kingdom restored","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 05-22-2016, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T09:05:04-07:00","id":896106,"title":"","content":"Are you looking at incorporating it as a story for the PCs to act out, a sort of cautionary tale to take place in the background with NPCs or as setting history?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T09:47:21-07:00","id":907683,"title":"","content":"Being mentioned a cautionary, or inspirational tale, but on the other issues, if you see use for the story I'll hear it<br /> <br /> as I always found it a inspiring tale of Hope and Redemption.<br /> <br /> Oh on the main topic on gifts, how do you think gift cards would be seen, would they be seen as an overly pedestrian gift?<br /> <br /> Although I could see an elder giving them to neonates their impressed with. <br /> <br /> Especialy one who seems promising but is struggling financialy<br /> <br /> any ideas what such a gift could mean beyond &quot;He likes you&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T07:05:24-07:00","id":910048,"title":"","content":"Gift cards, to me, would fall under context and intent. The fact that said elder took the time to personally handwrite a note, using expensive ink, on engraved stationary, imported from an exotic location and scented with an expensive perfume or cologne that is no longer produced by any company in the world, could actually be more monetarily valuable than a piece of jewelry with expertly cut gems. And that's just before you consider the fact that of sympathetic links that could be established with such a personalized item. Or the handwriting sample provided for potential future forgeries. (Like one of my characters has.)<br /> <br /> As a cautionary tale, I might incorporate as a background history for a current regent in the domain. I'll use the generic stereotypes but you can mix and match covenants to match your domains make up.<br /> Said regent was comparatively young (possibly a favored childe of the prince or primogen) but talented Invictus kindred who was granted regency based on that relationship. He ignored the warnings of a Sanctified ally about granting too many concessions to the Carthians, or indulging Masquerade violations by Acolytes and Dragons in the interest of promoting religious tolerance or thinking outside the box. He becomes popular with those groups (and alienates others) when he calls for the execution of a harpy on charges of sedition for blaming him and the prince for allowing them to get away with Masquerade violations and predicting that humans would be killing them in their sleep at this rate.<br /> Unsurprisingly, his 'tolerance' leads to a spike in attacks by hunters and a portion of his regency is usurped by his former Carthian supporters (their agenda all along). He re-dedicates himself to Sanctified teachings and Invictus policy, and reclaims his regency. He manages to nullify the hunter threat by turning them against the most egrarious Masquerade violators from the Circle and Ordo and uses that as leverage to reclaim his regency and re establish some alliances he would have alienated with his initial indiscretions. (This would likely have been some 20 odd years ago. Most of the hunters would be dead or retired/moved on to a real life by now.)<br /> <br /> If you want to up the ante and/or involve the players you could change things up slightly and say the Circle or Ordo conjured a nest of strix. (Two parents and a clutch of eggs that can't be destroyed by conventional methods.) The Circle or Ordo defends/conceals them. Eventually the story plays out with the strix parents being the ones stirring up hunter activity and getting killed. Your prototype Manassah and his Sanctified allies get a vision on the existence of the eggs and how to destroy them (submerge them in holy water prepared via an obscure ritual in Theban archives). Technically you could insert the PCs as any individual or faction but you run the risk of railroading them if they adopt adversarial roles to your Manassah although nothing says they can't switch sides in spite of covenant formal policies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 06-08-2016, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T10:46:22-07:00","id":914203,"title":"","content":"Hmmmn that sounds cool<br /> <br /> Hmmmn on Subtle insinuation in how you dress aany ideas how men can do so? I must be lacking an imagination because most of the examples I've seen on the issue have involved female kindred, wearing Dresses., like that one from the Invictus book<br /> <br /> Oh a scenariao that sprang into my head, well two scenariaos <br /> <br /> In both Someone commits dialbriee<br /> <br /> In one The prince is disgusted by the act but finds the perpeturrator absolutely indispensible, or feels that he , or the domain do owe him for past loyalty.<br /> <br /> In the other, he feels the act is quite justified, but feels he must give them some kind of minimalistic punishment to maintain appearances.<br /> <br /> Is their a way to communicate such feelings via innuendo anyone sees?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T18:59:05-07:00","id":916546,"title":"","content":"Color codes are popular. The Invictus and Ordo Dracul covenant books mention employing them, with certain colors being preferred by certain clan members or being off limits if you aren't a member of their respective sub groups. Certain colors have semi-universal meanings. (Blue signifies calm or peace, orange means superficial, etc.) Men could be somewhat unsubtle by having their suit be that color, or just restrict it to a handkerchief tucked into the breast pocket of their suit. Many different types of flowers also have certain connotations. (Something that could be pinned on a lapel or sent as a bouquet.) You could attach a form of locally understood phrases or statements to a particular brand of clothes or accessories (hats, cufflinks, shoes) or have them worn in combination with each other. Or something like wearing your clothes backwards or inside out. (Some cultures consider that a sign of impending bad or good luck.)<br /> <br /> Incidentally. the amaranth is not just a reference to soul eating, it's a flower. You could incorporate that into some sort of statement about diablerie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T10:37:05-07:00","id":916898,"title":"","content":"Mortal uniforms can be a statement to wear to Elysium, especially if it's something from your breathing days, personally, .<br /> <br /> All the jewelry, token, favor, and badge stuff is just as applicable to men as women. It also applies to symbols of faith, medals, rank identification, and ornamental weapons. A Cross of Confusion and a naked blade send a very different message than a crucifix and a peace knot, especially when the LeS is hosting. Politically minded Dragons may frown when one of their neonates arrives wearing a mortal keepsake.<br /> <br /> Cost is so obvious as to be forgotten, but that can be a big deal too. Unless you carry yourself particularly well, if you show up in a carefully pressed Goodwill suit people are probably going to assume you're either incompetent (&quot;I mean, good Lord, you can afford a tailored thousand-dollar suit over the normal course of <i>mugging your dinner</i> for a few nights, with care.&quot;), or you don't have the social experience to know you look incompetent, or you have no investment in the game.<br /> <br /> I'm gonna use an Estate hazing myself soon, where guests at events held by/for the most slovenly, unsuccessful, or unworthy junior Invictus surreptitiously mock them by wearing progressively cheaper and cheaper suits. The object of the game is to be the one with the cheapest suit when the host finally cottens on- if the cheapest suit is the one that made realization dawn, the second cheapest wins instead. Guests can stylishly opt themselves out of long-term games by showing up in outlandishly tattered or horrible suit as long as they have a believable reason for it, and it doesn't immediately alert the host. If the host NEVER catches on, the final event sees all the participating guests dressed like the host, as clumsily and unflatteringly as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 06-18-2016, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T21:08:30-07:00","id":1207146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/570983-advise-on-gifts\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/570983-advise-on-gifts\"> Advise on gifts - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/570983-advise-on-gifts\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/570983-advise-on-gifts </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Would like some advice on good gifts to give in various situations am STing my first Salon, what would a good gift to a Promising Invictus fledgling be? </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> sorry to bump this thread after so long but something I'm thinking on.<br /> <br /> is a Gift card a good gift to a ghoul to make them feel appreciated?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T04:02:32-07:00","id":1207213,"title":"","content":"It might, depending on the amount, location, financial situation of the ghoul and context. A Visa gift card for $200 may be considered a boon to a recently created ghoul who's a college student. Less so to a ghoul who's been around for ten years and already has access to their regnant's cars and bank accounts. Season tickets to a hockey team's home games may also be appreciated. Unless they vastly prefer another sport entirely or going out to the movies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T07:17:47-07:00","id":1207252,"title":"","content":"a $100 gift card to a fast food joint? to a ghoul thats overworked, and that you feel some small amount of empathy for?<br /> <br /> or is cash possibly better? <br /> <br /> <br /> oh? a Amaranth flower were giving to inform someone they'll be hunted for dialbriee soon?<br /> <br /> does giving it anonymously or personally sound better?<br /> <br /> problem with giving it personally, is they could report you to the Prince.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 04-15-2018, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T08:09:29-07:00","id":1207277,"title":"","content":"The gift card would be appropriate in that circumstance. Cash may be appreciated more because that's food of their choice or gas, a utility bill, etc.<br /> <br /> The amaranth flower would probably be construed as a warning more than a gift. Giving that anonymously may be safest politically for all involved parties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T09:57:02-07:00","id":1207308,"title":"","content":"ideas how say, giving a revolver could have different significane then a dagger?<br /> <br /> or a ornamental weapon different from a functional one? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Many gifts are meantt as iknnuendo<br /> <br /> <br /> like in one game I: ran on Rpol of Princess the hopeful, a rather vaingglorious troubadour of spades was trying to reform a Acolyte<br /> <br /> She tried to get him off her track by siccing him on a group of child porn distributors she also wanted taken down.<br /> <br /> but after managing to perform Cheval on him, she was able to find his real identity.<br /> <br /> and gave him a Sanxian, of expensive make at his home address to let him know she knew his real identity now.<br /> <br /> sadly the guy left before she could try aiming him at the chapel and the spear too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T16:08:22-07:00","id":1207434,"title":"","content":"I personally don\u2019t have characters give ornamental weapons as gifts except as an insult or threat. It\u2019s construed as an insult in that you think their martial skill is so poor that they won\u2019t notice the difference or their background knowledge in weapons collecting is shabby. That\u2019s just my interpretation though. Other possible symbolic meanings<br /> <br /> Dagger or a bottle of poison - an accusation of treachery<br /> Sword - a formal declaration of war<br /> Pistol(s) - formal challenge to duel <br /> <br /> Sometimes the symbolism could be a personal exchange of insults. One of my characters was sent a pure silver gun from a rival. It was a replica of the one she kept well hidden in an ankle holster. (How he knew about it drives straight into the realm of his sexual predatory behavior) Shortly afterwards, she was reprimanded over unnecessarily risking an Invictus financial portfolio in retaliation for a public insult his childe had levied at her during kindred court. This rival pulled strings to ensure she was publicly censured as well. After orchestrating her retaliation for that, said rival was sent a silver bullet .38 caliber made from the same silver as my character\u2019s replicated gun (melted down) with his name engraved on it. The next day one of his more influential organized crime boss retainers was arrested for racketeering. (And later shot before he could testify.)<br /> But later on, occasionally she would be gifted with a revolver and star badge in acknowledgement of her role as sheriff.(Or as a way of saying \u201cthank you for NOT killing someone\u201d even when she had legal cause) This same character was also sent a black rose once. At the time in the game there was a serial killer who\u2019s calling card was that he sent his victims a black rose three nights before he killed them. (Yes, vampires can be killed or torpored by solo serial killers in our setting.) A Carthian with pretensions of being a harpy tried to stir up drama and thought it would be funny to anonymously send them out as an empty threat to the female members of Invictus and was encouraged by an older Acolyte (who was actually trying to terrorize a Daeva neonate who had been kidnapped by hunters once) to send them. (The serial killer didn\u2019t consider imitation to be the sincerest form of flattery and eliminated their competition.)<br /> <br /> I had another character who gifted a real Cossack sword to a fellow House member after she had broken his ceremonial sword on his face a few hours before her inevitable embrace. There\u2019s a side story about him getting punished for years for being stupid enough to offer it to her in the first place but my character knows nothing about it. Their hostilities cooled eventually and my character, not knowing the one she broke was ceremonial, she thought she had broken a real one and eventually went through the trouble of replacing it with a real functional but antique one. <br /> Fast forward several years later, he becomes the prince and almost always wears the sword to public kindred functions and has performed a few executions with it. <br /> Anyone who asks about his sword will get regaled with the story of how his previous ceremonial sword was shattered trying to kill him by an insolent mortal. And he eventually got it replaced ten years later with a better sword. He then ends the story by introducing my character to the person as the Sword-breaker of his tale and as the one who gave him his vorpal sword. (That\u2019s what he calls it.) It has a twisted effect of either amusing kindred over my character being so naive to mistake a ceremonial sword for a real one, or horrifying them that she gave him an effective decapitation tool. (For some reason it\u2019s more believable to them that my character gave him a magical sword than the fact the he\u2019s obscenely strong and skilled in cutting off extremities.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T07:22:48-07:00","id":1207644,"title":"","content":"Thing about gifts that makes the calculus hard is, they're about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> 1. The recipient's present state, and background.<br /> 2. The giver's present state, and background.<br /> 3. Customs of the domain, and it's present state.<br /> 4. Any specifically intended message.<br /> <br /> Puzzling these out could be the work of several sessions of noodling for PCs, or a few die rolls for experienced characters. <br /> <br /> Case in point: a sword could just as easily represent an indication that the giver accepts the fealty of and responsibility for the recipient, for those with a more traditional, medievalist bent. It's a great present for an Invictus overlord to an actual underling. It's a provocation from an Invictus to anyone else--and if they don't see it that way, then those who do will wonder if the recipient has turned allegiances!<br /> <br /> Any other present can be equally complicated, especially if not explicitly explained. And what is the fun of that?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T07:36:27-07:00","id":1207654,"title":"","content":"oh ideas What a slave could represent?<br /> <br /> Say the Bull's mentioned in the invictus covenant book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T06:32:19-07:00","id":1216975,"title":"","content":"oh recently I bought a bright young woman on Facebook a hardcover of uncle tom's Cabin.<br /> <br /> <br /> And thought of getting some people who I disagree with a copy of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aunt_Phillis%27s_Cabin\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aunt_Phillis%27s_Cabin</a><br /> <br /> Can anyone see the symbolism there?<br /> <br /> a Hardcover makes it more meaningful, since you spent more money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T07:48:36-07:00","id":1216994,"title":"","content":"&gt;<br /> <br /> I can see some traditional symbolism but not without setting details for context. Uncle Tom\u2019s Cabin was supposed to be a screed against slavery with the protagonist being an example of a Christian others should emulate. The book promoted stereotypical portrayals of blacks and whites that persist to this day and currently blacks use the term \u201cUncle Tom\u201d as an insult to refer to other blacks who don\u2019t support the Democratic Party or aren\u2019t on board with demanding whites pay reparations for slavery or avidly maintaining a preference for African culture.<br /> <br /> Aunt Phillis\u2019 Cabin was supposed to be a counter argument against the stereotypes portrayed in Uncle Tom\u2019s Cabin. It was popular at the time but is not considered as influential as the former. Considering the fact that the themes and virtues of the main character of Uncle Tom\u2019s Cabin have been ignored so that being likened to the character is now a slur, it\u2019s not really surprising.<br /> <br /> From a VTR perspective, I could see either book being used as a reference to a faction that decides ghouling humans is not appropriate. I can easily envision a Sanctified/Carthian bloc adopting that stance, or even a younger Invictus faction composed of kindred who grew up in more contemporary times as a tactic to weaken their elders by kicking away their ghoul crutches.<br /> Either book could also be tossed around as a \u201cwarning\u201d towards Daeva with a propensity for enslaving their vessels or any other kindred who are a bit too liberal with blood bonds, and discipline application to make slaves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T08:24:39-07:00","id":1216999,"title":"","content":"aunt phyliss's cabin makes a major &quot;Mind your own business&quot; argument. And claims divine mandate because of the curse Noah laid on Ham.<br /> <br /> Is gifting the book a good way of saying &quot;Your logic is just as absurd&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T08:51:09-07:00","id":1217005,"title":"","content":"I'd like to point that &quot;Uncle Tom&quot; in modern usage seems to reference more the plays and subsequent movie, where the Tom character was changed to a black man who died for his white masters. Reading the book alone it might be harder to understand why the term became used as an insult.<br /> <br /> I'm not personally sure any of the above scenarios are really good examples of an Uncle Tom, and seem a little misinformed or biased, so I just want provide a counter opinion. The above description of the term is a bit reductive - it is used generally to label black people who are claimed to have 'turned their back on their people.' That can mean a broad range of things depending on who is doing the interpreting, but 'not demanding reparations' and 'not being an avid fan of African culture' are definitely not common examples imo.<br /> <br /> Okay, that's out of the way. I think the relative obscurity of Phylis' cabin means the symbolism is lost on most people, so it'd be more a matter of self-satisfaction than message-sending more often that not. Unless you of course have an educated audience, or an audience that might invest effort into interpreting the gift. (I mean, yeah. Send it to a member of the Sanctum and they might investigate what the hell it means. Send it to someone you met on facebook and they'll just be like 'that's weird, he sent me a gift'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T09:18:18-07:00","id":1217015,"title":"","content":"ideas on how to hint at what a gifts supposed to mean?<br /> <br /> like if you give someone a copy of &quot;The Prince&quot; it could mean &quot;You need to study it&quot; or &quot;Your truly worthy of Macchiavelli himself!&quot; <br /> <br /> (Sadly those for whom the first is the truth will all too often infer the latter) <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T09:20:35-07:00","id":1217017,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t get that message from Aunt Phillis\u2019 Cabin. If anything the story kind of struck me as the more realistic depiction of the prevailing mindset of how slavery really functioned and why it should persist (political and economic stability) as a foil to the unrealistic scenarios one dimensional character portrayals and extreme behavior to deliver the message in Uncle Tom\u2019s Cabin. They both rely on faulty premises and appeals to emotion over logic but Aunt Phillis\u2019 Cabin makes the more logical argument about \u201cminding your own business\u201d than Uncle Tom\u2019s Cabin did about the necessity to end slavery by sheer virtue of the fact that the latter doesn\u2019t even address the economic conditions a newly freed slave being required to provide everything for themself faces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T09:34:26-07:00","id":1217027,"title":"","content":"&quot;I think you and x character have a lot in common.&quot; is a good way to hint at a specific meaning in a book and encourage reading it. Not sure how well that works for Phillis' Cabin specifically.<br /> <br /> But usually the book's meaning is better if it's immediately obvious. Though I guess there is some benefit having the reciever work for the message.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T15:30:07-07:00","id":1217156,"title":"","content":"I take it that buying a copy of the Prince for anyone but a fledgeling is rude? as most vampires by that point are allready well versed in it and it could be taken as a snub.<br /> <br /> a Sire buying a nice leatherbound copy like mine might be showing affection though.trying to teach them to be an achiever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T19:23:57-07:00","id":1217240,"title":"","content":"It's funny you mention The Prince. One of my characters got into one of the backhanded gift incidents. And one of the NPCs decided to try and be witty and get involved in the exchange. She tried to gift that book to one of my characters in an elysium. I had my character promptly hand the book back and say &quot;I don't give autographs.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T15:14:08-07:00","id":1217505,"title":"","content":"Ideas on good things to get an enemy?<br /> <br /> I remember the Star Trek DS9 Episode &quot;The Wire&quot; Where Enabrim Tain creepys out Dr Bashir by offering him his favorite tea, served just the way he likes it.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on doing something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T17:32:31-07:00","id":1217538,"title":"","content":"That falls under the purview of pervert/stalker. It may creep out a relatively new vampire but I really don\u2019t envision it having the same effect on a vampire who\u2019s been around for awhile since there\u2019s an entire clan who\u2019s only real purpose and discipline spread gives them the ability to read your mind and sneak into your bedroom to rifle through your lingerie drawer with impunity. <br /> <br /> You don\u2019t creep them out by issuing veiled insults. You creep them out/piss them off by befriending or doing favors for the nonkindred people who hold some significance to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T17:57:45-07:00","id":1217545,"title":"","content":"Oh think theirs collector's or luxary editions of the Testament of Loginius for the vain or spendthrift sanctified?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T04:00:28-07:00","id":1217612,"title":"","content":"Is the Testament of Longinus mass produced in your setting? If yes, then possibly. Otherwise merely owning a copy may be a luxury in and of itself where it could be as extravagant or spartan as the one who commissions its printing or transcribing it wants it to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T07:20:28-07:00","id":1217653,"title":"","content":"thought it was a valid question.<br /> <br /> Think a fair share of the laity and those only tenatively considering conversion will keep their copys of the book electronicly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T09:36:09-07:00","id":1217692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/570983-advise-on-gifts?p=1217653#post1217653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thought it was a valid question.<br /> <br /> Think a fair share of the laity and those only tenatively considering conversion will keep their copys of the book electronicly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wasn't thinking electronically. I was thinking of the logistics and practicalities of producing a book prior to the 1990s where printers and scanners were finally affordable household items. Copies of the Testament of Longinius were most likely going to be produced at a local level by a Sanctified kindred who had a printing press or the skills of a traditional bookbinder and scribe. (And thereby subject to censorship and distribution regulations that prevailed in the area.) Even today decent large multi-function print and scan machines that are used for print on demand services run close to half a million dollars a piece. So quality is going to be subjective.<br /> Alternatively your setting could have some sort of underground kindred text printing service that has a printing press and mail distribution service to deliver kindred specific texts all over the world that would likely be regulated to ensure copies don't fall into non kindred hands or are used by kindred factions sworn to tear down the Masquerade. In this case you may well have limited edition copies signed by the great great great grandchilde of the Monachus or some other Sanctified celebrity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 05-11-2018, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T01:38:34-07:00","id":1217913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/570983-advise-on-gifts?p=1217692#post1217692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively your setting could have some sort of underground kindred text printing service that has a printing press and mail distribution service to deliver kindred specific texts all over the world that would likely be regulated to ensure copies don't fall into non kindred hands or are used by kindred factions sworn to tear down the Masquerade. In this case you may well have limited edition copies signed by the great great great grandchilde of the Monachus or some other Sanctified celebrity.</div> </div> </div> </div>To expand on this idea, in such a case it would make sense for each copy to contain a serial number (preferably on important pages so it can't easily be removed) and the printing service to keep a record of who's ordered each specific copy. It can also be made more difficult (but definitely far from impossible) for people to bluff themselves into getting a copy if orders requires referrals from already recognized Kindred.<br /> I'm pretty sure that's what you meant by &quot;regulated&quot; so maybe not actually expanded much but writing it out anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-12-2018, 04:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T10:28:01-07:00","id":1219302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/570983-advise-on-gifts?p=1217538#post1217538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That falls under the purview of pervert/stalker. It may creep out a relatively new vampire but I really don\u2019t envision it having the same effect on a vampire who\u2019s been around for awhile since there\u2019s an entire clan who\u2019s only real purpose and discipline spread gives them the ability to read your mind and sneak into your bedroom to rifle through your lingerie drawer with impunity.<br /> <br /> You don\u2019t creep them out by issuing veiled insults. You creep them out/piss them off by befriending or doing favors for the nonkindred people who hold some significance to them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> would that work better with hunter's?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T10:38:03-07:00","id":1219305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/570983-advise-on-gifts?p=1219302#post1219302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> would that work better with hunter's?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if they're human vampire hunters it would probably creep them out to where they might consider abandoning their hobby. Or it might inspire the hunter to take a more proactive approach to dealing with vampires once and for all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"k